const H=1.1,e="case-05",I=5,t="The Understudy's Secret",o="A Bizzing mystery",P=2,n="playhouse",a="the Playhouse Quarter, the open-air Playhouse, the night before opening",s=["voice","inference","sequence","detail"],r="NEVER",L=5,i={id:"green-pen",name:"a green pen",art:"Celeste's green pen"},h=[{thread:"A",beat:"NEVER vanishes from the Playhouse poster; a calling card in the prompt book; the Blot Ledger reads UNDER · THE · CLOCK · THAT · NEVER",docs:["5.5","5.arc.card"]},{thread:"C",beat:"the second Raman postcard, from Nairobi, a dated list proving Crane and Co bought and closed two libraries",docs:["5.6"]},{thread:"C",beat:"Felix discovers he is happy in the hidden prompt corner (set-up for his reveal speech in Case 7)",docs:[]}],l=[],d={text:`Curtain up is tomorrow at seven.
But tonight the star's script has vanished from a room nobody entered.
Someone has underlined green lines in the understudy's script.
A note with no name says, "Learn the green lines."
Is Hugo stealing the lead? Was it Petra? Or the cat who will not move?`,readAloud:!0,clock:"Curtain up: tomorrow at seven (shown as a ticket stub in the card corner)"},c=[{panel:1,place:"the open-air Playhouse, Friday, 8 pm",picture:"The open-air Playhouse at dusk, the painted lighthouse on stage with its lamp dark, lanterns along the empty seats, programmes lifting in the sea wind.",caption:"Friday, 8 pm. Curtain up: tomorrow at seven.",lines:[]},{panel:2,place:"backstage",picture:"Backstage: Petra with her clipboard, pointing at an empty dressing table.",lines:[{who:"PETRA",text:"Curtain up tomorrow at seven. No script, no Keeper. No Keeper, no show."}]},{panel:3,place:"backstage",picture:"Hugo holding his script up, green lines on the page, looking horrified.",lines:[{who:"HUGO",text:"I didn't do this! Sorry. I mean, I didn't."}]},{panel:4,place:"backstage",picture:"Encore asleep on a costume basket, one ear folded, refusing to move for anyone. Behind him, a dressing-room door with a painted star, firmly shut.",caption:"Nobody went through that door all evening.",lines:[]},{panel:5,place:"the stage door",picture:"The agency at the stage door.",lines:[{who:"NELL",text:"Understudy. Wants the lead. Hunch-o-meter: ten!"},{who:"QUILL",text:"Show me where it says that."}]}],p=[{who:"STAGE",text:"Nell pins Hugo's portrait in the middle."},{who:"NELL",text:"He wants the part, and he's got the lines underlined. Hunch-o-meter: ten!"},{who:"FELIX",text:"Footnote: an *understudy* learns a part in case the lead can't go on. Footnote to the footnote: learning it isn't stealing it."},{who:"QUILL",text:"Show me where it says Hugo took anything."},{who:"PETRA",direction:"from the prompt corner, without looking up",text:"Forty minutes to nine."}],u=[{id:"hugo",name:"Hugo Aldana",role:"suspect",note:"the understudy",look:"early twenties, curly hair that will not stay flat, a too-long knitted scarf, a bus ticket always poking out of a pocket.",manner:"eager, sweet, says sorry far too often. Knows every line of every part, including the cat's (there is no cat's part).",expressions:["calm","nervous","offended","amused","guilty","relieved"],unlockedBy:null,motive:"wants the lead, and the green lines are in *his* script",secret:'his "late bus" is a white lie: every evening he reads the whole play aloud to his gran at Harbour House, because she cannot come to opening night.'},{id:"petra",name:"Petra Nwosu",role:"suspect",note:"stage manager",look:"headset round her neck, a pencil behind each ear, a clipboard, black clothes, sensible boots.",manner:"brisk, exact, secretly very kind. Talks in lists. Writes everything down, including the cat.",expressions:["calm","offended","nervous","amused","guilty","relieved"],unlockedBy:null,motive:"if the star cannot go on, it is Petra's job to say who does, and she can see every door from her corner",secret:"she has known about Celeste's voice since Tuesday, and promised to tell no one."},{id:"encore",name:"Encore",role:"suspect",note:"the stage-door cat, Inkwell's most famous cat",look:"large, ginger and white, one ear folded, a velvet collar from an old costume.",manner:"sleeps on whatever matters most. Has been in more shows than anyone. Answers no questions.",expressions:["asleep","one-eye-open","offended","amused","smug","yawning"],unlockedBy:null,motive:"he sleeps on whatever matters most",secret:"he knows exactly where the script is, because he is lying on it."},{id:"celeste",name:"Celeste Fairweather",role:"culprit-hidden",note:"the lead, playing the Keeper",look:"sixties, silver hair in a soft knot, a long green shawl, a green pen behind one ear.",manner:'warm, grand, funny, calls everyone "dear". Tonight she only whispers, and writes instead of talking.',expressions:["calm","nervous","offended","amused","guilty","relieved"],unlockedBy:"D1",motive:"twenty years on that stage without missing a single show",secret:"her voice went on Tuesday, and only Petra knows."},{id:"quill",name:"Quill",role:"agency",look:"in the deerstalker",manner:"whispers grammar corrections in the dark.",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null},{id:"nell",name:"Nell Okafor-Hart",role:"agency",look:"",manner:"hunch-o-meter at ten before she reaches the stage door.",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null},{id:"asha",name:"Asha Raman",role:"agency",look:"",manner:"timeline on the back of a programme. Checks the postcard's dates.",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null},{id:"dev",name:"Dev Raman",role:"agency",look:"",manner:"solves the postcard puzzle; spots that word patterns repeat. Has the best nose in the agency.",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null},{id:"felix",name:"Felix Moreno-Lindqvist",role:"agency",look:"",manner:"footnotes about green ink and understudies. Discovers the prompt corner.",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null},{id:"tully",name:"Constable Bram Tully",role:"helper",look:"",manner:"ten minutes behind, with the cocoa. Rode the number four bus tonight. Biscuit is missing again.",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null},{id:"rosalind",name:"Rosalind Ashe",role:"witness",look:"Ink on her cuffs, pencil in her hair. Small figure.",manner:"the Playhouse's writer. Sets the deadline in chapter 2; appears in the reveal and epilogue.",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null},{id:"sunny",name:"Sunny",role:"witness",look:"Small figure.",manner:"the lighting operator (seen briefly; returns in Case 7).",expressions:[],unlockedBy:null}],g=[{id:"5.1",chapter:"scene",type:"log",title:"Petra's stage log",author:"Petra Nwosu, stage manager",when:"Friday evening",where:"the prompt corner, clipped to the prompt book",picture:"a ruled log sheet on a clipboard, small square capitals, a pencil on a string.",readAloud:!1,body:`LOG · Friday
5.30 Celeste in. Whispers she is [[c:log-saving|saving her voice]].
5.45 [[c:log-honey|Honey and lemon sent up]].
6.00 [[c:log-table|Script on her table]].
6.30 [[c:log-alone|Celeste alone in her room. Door shut]].
6.40 [[c:log-shawl|Celeste's shawl into the costume basket]].
6.45 [[c:log-light|Light check on stage. Me and Sunny]].
7.00 [[c:log-gone|Celeste's script GONE!]]
7.15 [[c:log-hugo|Hugo in. Bus late]].
7.20 [[c:log-note|Hugo brings me a green note]]. Pale.
All night: [[c:log-cat|Encore asleep in the costume basket]].`,gloss:{"prompt corner":"the hidden place at the side of the stage where the stage manager runs the show and whispers forgotten lines."},footnote:{who:"QUILL",text:"'Sunny and I.' Not 'me and Sunny.' Carry on."}},{id:"5.2",chapter:"scene",type:"note",title:"The green note",author:"unsigned",when:"undated",where:"tucked inside the cover of Hugo's script, on his chair",picture:"a cream card, green ink, big looping letters, one tiny green smudge after the final dash.",readAloud:!1,body:`[[c:note-dear|Hugo dear]],
Learn the green lines tonight. [[c:note-simply|Simply all of them]].
They will be yours on Saturday.
[[c:note-splendid|You will be splendid]].
Please do not ask why.
And please do not tell a soul.
[[c:note-friend|Your friend —]]`},{id:"5.3",chapter:"scene",type:"other",title:"Script page 12, with green underlines",author:"Rosalind Ashe (the play); the green underlines by an unknown hand",when:"—",where:"Hugo's understudy script, page 12, open on his chair",picture:"a typed script page, a coffee ring, some lines underlined in green ink, a green note in the margin.",readAloud:!1,body:`*The Lighthouse Keeper's Daughter*, by Rosalind Ashe. Act One.
LARK: Mother, the storm is coming.
KEEPER: <u>Then we climb. Ninety-nine steps, and a lamp at the top.</u>
<u>A ship we cannot see is still a ship.</u>
LARK: Who will thank us?
KEEPER: Nobody, my love.
KEEPER: <u>That is how you know it matters. Now hold the rail.</u>
*(Green ink, in the margin:)* [[c:page-long|All the long ones are yours, dear]].`,underlineColour:"green"},{id:"5.4",chapter:"scene",type:"card",title:"Celeste's card to Petra",author:"Celeste Fairweather",when:"Wednesday",where:"pinned to the cork board in the prompt corner, among cue sheets",picture:"a cream card with a painted gull, green ink, the same big looping letters.",readAloud:!1,body:`[[c:card-dear|Petra dear]],
[[c:card-simply|Simply splendid work]] on the storm scene!
The thunder made me jump. The rain made me cry.
Thank you, thank you.
[[c:card-could|I would shout it from the lamp room, if I could]].
[[c:card-friend|Your friend —C.]]`,note:`The clue in plain sight: "I would shout it from the lamp room" reads like an actor's flourish, and it is literal. Dated Wednesday; her voice went on Tuesday, so she wrote her thanks.`},{id:"5.5",chapter:"scene",type:"poster",title:"The Playhouse poster",author:"the Playhouse",when:"printed last month",where:"on the stage door",picture:"a painted poster of the lighthouse beam across a stormy sea; a neat slip of cream paper covers one word. All poster text is live type, never painted.",readAloud:!1,body:`THE PLAYHOUSE PRESENTS
*The Lighthouse Keeper's Daughter*
A new play by Rosalind Ashe
Starring Celeste Fairweather as the Keeper
[[c:poster-years|Twenty years on our stage]], and [[c:poster-gap|she has ____ missed a show]]!
Opening Saturday at seven.`},{id:"5.6",chapter:"scene",type:"postcard",title:"Leela's postcard from Nairobi",author:"Dr Leela Raman",when:"postmarked Nairobi, Monday",where:"arrived at the agency by the bakery dumbwaiter, with the cinnamon buns, just before the agency set out",picture:"the front shows acacia trees at sunset and giraffes on the horizon; the back has a stamp with a sunbird and Leela's quick, slanting writing.",readAloud:!1,body:`Jambo, my two detectives!
Today I found Crane and Co's old company papers.
Your puzzle: put my list in date order.
[[c:pc-larkclose|9 June: Larkhill Library closes]]. New sign: "The Larkhill Experience".
[[c:pc-larkbuy|2 February: Crane and Co buys Larkhill Library]].
[[c:pc-fenclose|1 March: Fenwick Library closes]]. New sign: "The Fenwick Experience".
[[c:pc-fenbuy|14 November last year: Crane and Co buys Fenwick Library]].
What comes next on this list?
Love, Mum`,arcThread:"C"},{id:"5.arc.card",chapter:"arc",type:"card",title:"The Blot's calling card",author:"B.",when:"Friday evening",where:"found by Petra between two pages of the prompt book",picture:"a small cream card, a perfect round ink blot.",readAloud:!1,body:`A voice can be lost.
A voice can be found on paper.
— B.`,arcThread:"A",talk:[{who:"STAGE",text:"Dev holds the card to his nose."},{who:"DEV",text:"Pine trees? No. Sharper."},{who:"FELIX",text:"Footnote: that's rosin. Violinists rub it on their bows so the strings will sing. Footnote to the footnote: there is no violin in this play."},{who:"STAGE",text:"Nobody says anything. Then, from somewhere out in the dark seats, soft as a draught, someone plays three notes on a violin, and stops. Petra throws up the house lights. Every seat is empty. The programmes lift and settle in the wind."},{who:"TULLY",text:"The wind."},{who:"QUILL",text:"The wind does not play in tune."}]},{id:"5.S1.Q1",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Hugo Aldana: "When did you get to the Playhouse tonight?"',author:"Hugo Aldana",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`A quarter past seven. I'm so sorry.
The number four bus broke down by the bridge.
I ran the rest of the way.
Petra wrote it down. She writes everything down.`},{id:"5.S1.Q2",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Hugo Aldana: "What did you find on your chair?"',author:"Hugo Aldana",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`My script, open at page twelve.
Green lines all over the Keeper's speeches.
And a card tucked in the cover.
I didn't write it! I don't even own a green pen.
I took it straight to Petra.`},{id:"5.S1.Q3",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Hugo Aldana: "Do you want to play the Keeper?"',author:"Hugo Aldana",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`Every understudy dreams about it. Of course I do.
But not like this. Not by taking someone's script.
Celeste taught me how to bow.
I'd never steal from her.`},{id:"5.S1.Q4",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Hugo Aldana: "Can we see something you wrote?"',author:"Hugo Aldana",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`*(He hands over a note he left for Petra on Thursday.)*
[[c:hugo-note|petra — sorry sorry]]. bus late again.
i'll learn act two on the way home.
really sorry. h`},{id:"5.S1.Q5",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Hugo Aldana: "Who do you think wrote the green note?"',author:"Hugo Aldana",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`Someone who believes in me, I suppose.
That's the strange part. It's a kind note.
Thieves don't usually say "you will be splendid".`},{id:"5.S1.Q6",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Hugo Aldana: "Why did you say the bus was late?"',author:"Hugo Aldana (with Constable Tully)",when:"Friday night, twenty to nine",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript; a bus ticket clipped to the corner.",readAloud:!1,body:`TULLY: [[c:tully-bus|The number four ran on time tonight]]. I was on it.
HUGO: [[c:hugo-lie|I wasn't on the bus]]. Sorry.
I was at Harbour House, with my gran.
She can't come tomorrow, so I read her the play. Every part.
I made up a part for the cat. She likes the cat.
[[c:hugo-gran|Matron signed me in at half past five and out at ten to seven]].
Then I ran.`,talk:[{who:"NELL",direction:"very quietly",text:"Wrong again."},{who:"ASHA",text:"So he wasn't in the building at all between six and seven. He was across town with a matron and a gran."},{who:"HUGO",direction:"to the child",text:"An actor who rehearses for his gran. I thought everyone would laugh."},{who:"STAGE",text:"Nobody laughs."}]},{id:"5.S2.Q1",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:`Petra Nwosu: "When did you last see Celeste's script?"`,author:"Petra Nwosu",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`Six o'clock. On her table. I check every table at six.
At seven it was gone.
[[c:petra-search|I searched that room from the mirror to the mat. Nothing.]]
In between, I was on stage with Sunny.
We were checking every light for the storm scene.`},{id:"5.S2.Q2",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Petra Nwosu: "Do you ever use green ink?"',author:"Petra Nwosu",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`Not in my prompt corner.
Some actors say green is unlucky on stage.
I use pencil. Pencil rubs out. Mistakes happen.
[[c:petra-green|Only one person here writes in green]].
But that's her own business.`},{id:"5.S2.Q3",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:`Petra Nwosu: "Who went into Celeste's room tonight?"`,author:"Petra Nwosu",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`Only Celeste.
[[c:petra-nobody|I can see her door from my corner and from the stage. Nobody went in]].
[[c:petra-shawl|She came out once, with only her shawl over her arm]].
She has been whispering since Tuesday.
She says she is just resting her voice.`,note:"Petra chooses her words like a person carrying something full to the brim. She does not lie. She keeps a promise."},{id:"5.S2.Q4",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Petra Nwosu: "What about the card in your prompt book?"',author:"Petra Nwosu",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`I found it at half past seven. It wasn't there at six.
A little ink blot, very neat.
I don't know who left it.
I do know the cat didn't. The cat can't open books.`},{id:"5.S2.Q5",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Petra Nwosu: "Where is Encore now?"',author:"Petra Nwosu",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`Still in the costume basket.
He climbed in just before the light check.
He won't move. I've tried a sardine.
When a cat won't move off something, it's usually something warm.`},{id:"5.S3.Q1",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:`Encore, the stage-door cat: "Where were you at seven o'clock?"`,author:"Encore, the stage-door cat",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`*(Encore opens one eye.)*
*(He closes it again.)*
PETRA: In the costume basket. Same as now.`},{id:"5.S3.Q2",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:`Encore, the stage-door cat: "Did you take Celeste's script?"`,author:"Encore, the stage-door cat",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`*(Encore yawns. He turns round three times on the basket.)*
*(He lies down exactly where he was before.)*
TULLY: I'll put that down as a no.`},{id:"5.S3.Q3",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:`Encore, the stage-door cat: "Why won't you get out of the basket?"`,author:"Encore, the stage-door cat",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`*(Encore puts one paw firmly on a green shawl.)*
*(He purrs, very loudly.)*
PETRA: He's guarding something. He always guards Celeste's things.`},{id:"5.S3.Q4",chapter:"interview",type:"transcript",title:'Encore, the stage-door cat: "Who is your favourite person in the Playhouse?"',author:"Encore, the stage-door cat",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a typed transcript.",readAloud:!1,body:`*(Encore looks past everyone, to the dressing room with the shut door.)*
PETRA: Celeste. He sits on her lap at every rehearsal.`},{id:"5.S4.Q1",chapter:"interview",type:"card",title:'Celeste Fairweather: "Where is your script?"',author:"Celeste Fairweather",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a card in green ink.",readAloud:!1,body:`Gone, dear. Simply gone.
Do not fuss about it.
The show will be splendid.
—C.`},{id:"5.S4.Q2",chapter:"interview",type:"card",title:'Celeste Fairweather: "Why are you whispering?"',author:"Celeste Fairweather",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a card in green ink.",readAloud:!1,body:`Resting my voice, dear. Simply resting.
Actors do it all the time.
[[c:celeste-never|Twenty years, and I have not missed one show]].
I do not intend to start now.
—C.`},{id:"5.S4.Q3",chapter:"interview",type:"card",title:'Celeste Fairweather: "Did you write a note to Hugo?"',author:"Celeste Fairweather",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a card in green ink.",readAloud:!1,body:`*(She looks at the card for a long time before she writes.)*
Why would anyone ask that?
Hugo is a dear boy.
He knows every line in the play.
—C.`},{id:"5.S4.Q4",chapter:"interview",type:"card",title:'Celeste Fairweather: "When did you go to the costume basket?"',author:"Celeste Fairweather",when:"Friday night",where:"the green room",picture:"a card in green ink.",readAloud:!1,body:`Twenty to seven, perhaps.
I put my shawl away. It was too warm.
Is that a crime now, dear?
—C.`}],w=[{suspect:"hugo",questions:[{id:"hugo-q1",type:"when",q:"When did you get to the Playhouse tonight?",answerDoc:"5.S1.Q1",expression:"nervous"},{id:"hugo-q2",type:"what",q:"What did you find on your chair?",answerDoc:"5.S1.Q2",expression:"offended"},{id:"hugo-q3",type:"why",q:"Do you want to play the Keeper?",answerDoc:"5.S1.Q3",expression:"guilty"},{id:"hugo-q4",type:"what",q:"Can we see something you wrote?",answerDoc:"5.S1.Q4",expression:"calm"},{id:"hugo-q5",type:"who",q:"Who do you think wrote the green note?",answerDoc:"5.S1.Q5",expression:"amused"},{id:"hugo-q6",type:"why",q:"Why did you say the bus was late?",answerDoc:"5.S1.Q6",expression:"guilty",expressionThen:"relieved",unlockedAt:"chapter 4",unlockedBy:"the end of chapter 3 (Tully's bus)"}]},{suspect:"petra",questions:[{id:"petra-q1",type:"when",q:"When did you last see Celeste's script?",answerDoc:"5.S2.Q1",expression:"calm"},{id:"petra-q2",type:"what",q:"Do you ever use green ink?",answerDoc:"5.S2.Q2",expression:"offended"},{id:"petra-q3",type:"who",q:"Who went into Celeste's room tonight?",answerDoc:"5.S2.Q3",expression:"nervous"},{id:"petra-q4",type:"what",q:"What about the card in your prompt book?",answerDoc:"5.S2.Q4",expression:"nervous"},{id:"petra-q5",type:"where",q:"Where is Encore now?",answerDoc:"5.S2.Q5",expression:"amused"}]},{suspect:"encore",questions:[{id:"encore-q1",type:"where",q:"Where were you at seven o'clock?",answerDoc:"5.S3.Q1",expression:"one-eye-open"},{id:"encore-q2",type:"what",q:"Did you take Celeste's script?",answerDoc:"5.S3.Q2",expression:"yawning"},{id:"encore-q3",type:"why",q:"Why won't you get out of the basket?",answerDoc:"5.S3.Q3",expression:"smug"},{id:"encore-q4",type:"who",q:"Who is your favourite person in the Playhouse?",answerDoc:"5.S3.Q4",expression:"amused"}]},{suspect:"celeste",questions:[{id:"celeste-q1",type:"where",q:"Where is your script?",answerDoc:"5.S4.Q1",expression:"calm"},{id:"celeste-q2",type:"why",q:"Why are you whispering?",answerDoc:"5.S4.Q2",expression:"offended"},{id:"celeste-q3",type:"what",q:"Did you write a note to Hugo?",answerDoc:"5.S4.Q3",expression:"nervous"},{id:"celeste-q4",type:"when",q:"When did you go to the costume basket?",answerDoc:"5.S4.Q4",expression:"guilty"}],unlockedBy:"D1"}],y=[{id:"D1",type:"voice",skill:"voice",statement:"The green note was written by Celeste. It sounds like her card to Petra, not like Hugo's notes.",spans:["note-dear","card-dear","note-simply","card-simply","note-splendid","note-friend","card-friend","hugo-note","petra-green"],pairs:[["note-dear","card-dear"],["note-simply","card-simply"],["note-friend","card-friend"]],contrastSpans:["hugo-note"],supportingSpans:["petra-green"],why:`writers leave fingerprints in words. Celeste always puts "dear" after a name, uses the word "simply", and signs "Your friend —C." The note does all three, and stops at the dash, as if she began to sign and remembered not to. Hugo writes in lower case and says sorry; Petra writes in lists. The green note is Celeste's.`,unlocks:"celeste"},{id:"D2",type:"inference",skill:"inference",statement:"Celeste is losing her voice and is too proud and embarrassed to say so. She marked the long speeches for Hugo because she cannot manage them, and she hid her own script because it would give her secret away.",spans:["log-saving","log-honey","page-long","poster-gap","poster-years","celeste-never","card-could"],supportingSpans:["celeste-never","card-could"],why:`nobody says "I've lost my voice" anywhere in the documents. The child has to put it together: whispering, honey and lemon, long speeches handed over while short lines are kept, and a thank-you *written* on Wednesday by a woman who always says it out loud. And the poster explains the silence: twenty years without missing a show is a lot to be proud of, and a lot to lose. Once the gap is filled (NEVER), the motive is plain.`},{id:"D3",type:"timeline",skill:"sequence",statement:"The script vanished between six and seven, while Celeste was alone in her room and Petra was on stage. Hugo arrived after it had gone. So Hugo could not have taken it.",spans:["log-table","log-alone","log-gone","log-hugo","log-light","petra-nobody","petra-shawl","petra-search"],supportingSpans:["log-light","petra-nobody","petra-shawl","petra-search"],why:"the green note and the underlines were waiting for Hugo when he arrived at 7.15. The script was already gone at 7.00. Only Celeste was in her own room in that hour, and ten minutes after the door shut she carried her shawl to the costume basket.",impossible:{question:'The script was on the table at six. Nobody went into the room. Petra searched it at seven, mirror to mat, and the script was not there. The only person who came out was Celeste, once, "with only her shawl over her arm". So how did a whole script leave a room that nobody entered?',answer:"It went out of the room inside the shawl, and into the costume basket, where Encore lay on it because it was warm.",spans:["log-shawl","petra-shawl"],alsoQuoted:`5.S2.Q5: "When a cat won't move off something, it's usually something warm."`,answeredIn:"the reveal"}},{id:"D-arc",type:"timeline",skill:"sequence",optional:!0,decidesCase:!1,arcThread:"C",file:"Crane",statement:"Crane and Co buys a library, and about four months later it closes.",spans:["pc-fenbuy","pc-larkbuy","pc-fenclose","pc-larkclose"],order:["pc-fenbuy","pc-larkbuy","pc-fenclose","pc-larkclose"],extraSkills:["detail"],note:"Arc link (optional, not one of the three).",why:"Filed under *Crane* in the notebook; it earns credit for `sequence` but does not decide this case."}],m=[{suspect:"hugo",clearedBy:["log-hugo","log-gone","hugo-note","hugo-gran"],note:`Wants the part; the underlines are in his script. The green lines are all the Keeper's speeches, in *his* copy. The note says "They will be yours on Saturday." And at the end of chapter 3 Tully proves the bus was on time, which Hugo admits. Cleared: he arrived after the script was gone; his voice is nothing like the note's; and Matron had him at Harbour House for the whole hour (chapter 4).`,suspicion:["tully-bus","hugo-lie"],falseSolution:!0,secret:"He reads the play to his gran every evening, and was too shy to say so."},{suspect:"petra",clearedBy:["log-light","petra-green"],note:"The calling card was in *her* prompt book; she was alone in the prompt corner; she is plainly keeping something back. She was on stage, with a witness; she writes in pencil, in lists.",secret:"She has known about Celeste's voice since Tuesday, and kept her promise. What she held back was a friend's secret, not a script."},{suspect:"encore",clearedBy:["log-cat"],pointsTo:["log-shawl"],note:"Comic; he will not move off the costume basket. Asleep all night; common sense, with Tully's help: a cat cannot write in green ink. (Tully checks his paws anyway. They are clean.) The joke that is also a clue: a cat who won't move is sitting on something warm and important.",secret:"He knows where the script is: underneath him."}],b={events:[{id:"T1",order:1,text:"Celeste arrives, croaky and whispering.",spans:["log-saving"],placedByChild:!1,when:"5.30"},{id:"T2",order:2,text:"Honey and lemon go up to her room.",spans:["log-honey"],placedByChild:!1,when:"5.45"},{id:"T3",order:3,text:"Petra checks: the script is on Celeste's table.",spans:["log-table"],placedByChild:!0,when:"6.00"},{id:"T4",order:4,text:"Celeste shuts herself in her room, alone. She underlines Hugo's script and writes the note.",spans:["log-alone"],placedByChild:!0,when:"6.30"},{id:"T5",order:5,text:"Celeste takes her shawl, and her script wrapped inside it, to the costume basket.",spans:["log-shawl"],placedByChild:!0,when:"6.40"},{id:"T6",order:6,text:"Encore climbs into the basket and settles on the shawl.",spans:[],placedByChild:!1,when:"just before the light check",source:"5.S2.Q5"},{id:"T7",order:7,text:"Petra and Sunny check the lights on stage.",spans:["log-light"],placedByChild:!1,when:"6.45"},{id:"T8",order:8,text:"Matron signs Hugo out of Harbour House, and he runs for the Playhouse.",spans:["hugo-gran"],placedByChild:!0,when:"6.50"},{id:"T9",order:9,text:"Petra finds the script gone.",spans:["log-gone"],placedByChild:!0,when:"7.00"},{id:"T10",order:10,text:"Hugo arrives, late, and finds the green lines and the note.",spans:["log-hugo"],placedByChild:!0,when:"7.15"},{id:"T11",order:11,text:"Hugo takes the green note straight to Petra.",spans:["log-note"],placedByChild:!1,when:"7.20"}],join:{before:"T9",after:["T10"],deduction:"D3",wrong:{who:"ASHA",text:"Can't take a thing that's already gone. That's not detective work, that's magic."},note:"Event 9 (gone) is pegged before event 10 (Hugo arrives), and Hugo's whole hour is at Harbour House."},runningJoke:{who:"ASHA",text:"7.40 arrive. 7.41 cat. 7.42 cat refuses. 7.43 cocoa."},arcPuzzle:{deduction:"D-arc",order:["pc-fenbuy","pc-larkbuy","pc-fenclose","pc-larkclose"]},intro:'The washing line is strung across the green room (which is still not green). Petra calls the time as the pegs go on: "Twenty to nine."'},f={question:"Who hid Celeste's script, and wrote the green note?",culprit:"celeste",place:null,minimalEvidence:["D1","D2","D3"],acceptableEvidence:["note-friend","card-friend","log-saving","page-long","log-alone","log-gone"],wrongSuspect:{hugo:"Forget the bus. Where was he from half past five till ten to seven, and who signed him out? And when was the script already gone?",petra:"Where was she at quarter to seven, and who was with her? And what does she write with?",encore:"A fine suspect. A terrible writer. Read where he spent the evening."},wrongSuspectPoints:{hugo:["hugo-gran","log-gone"],petra:["log-light","petra-green"],encore:["log-cat"]},weakEvidence:"You've chosen the right person, but you haven't shown it yet. Whose *words* are these? *Why* would she do it? And *when* could she? Three pins.",note:"She hid her own script and wrote the note, to hand her long speeches to Hugo without admitting that she has lost her voice.",evidenceRule:{minimalEvidenceRule:"three pins, one from each deduction",evidenceGroups:{D1:["note-friend","card-friend"],D2:["log-saving","page-long"],D3:["log-alone","log-gone"]}},wrongTheory:{"the Blot":"The Blot takes one word at a time and leaves the gap tidy. A whole script is not a word. Read the log: who came out of that room, and what was over her arm?"}},k=[{who:"QUILL",text:"Ten minutes. New detective, take them through it."},{who:"NELL",text:"*(to the child)* You read it. You say it. *(beat)* Fine, I'll start. Hugo didn't take anything."},{who:"ASHA",text:"Matron had him at Harbour House until ten to seven. The script was gone at seven. He was still running."},{who:"HUGO",text:"Reading to my gran. Sorry. I mean, not sorry."},{who:"NELL",text:"Petra was on stage with Sunny. But she was hiding something."},{who:"PETRA",text:"*(quietly)* I knew about the voice. She made me promise. I didn't know about the script."},{who:"FELIX",text:`So it's the voice. Not the speaking one, the writing one. "Hugo dear." "Petra dear." "Simply all of them." "Simply splendid." Footnote: everyone has words they can't stop using. Footnote to the footnote: mine is "footnote".`},{who:"DEV",text:'*(holding the note beside the card)* The card ends "Your friend —C." The note ends "Your friend —" and stops. Someone began to sign, then remembered not to.'},{who:"STAGE",text:"Everyone turns. Celeste stands very still. She pulls the green pen from behind her ear, and writes."},{who:"CELESTE",text:'*(the card, read aloud by Petra)* "Yes. It was me. —C."'},{who:"NELL",text:"But nobody went into that room. And you came out with nothing!"},{who:"QUILL",text:"Nothing but a shawl. Read the log. Where did the shawl go?"},{who:"STAGE",text:"Nell kneels by the costume basket."},{who:"NELL",text:"The cat's laying on it!"},{who:"QUILL",text:"*Lying.* Hens lay eggs. Cats lie on scripts. Lift him gently."},{who:"STAGE",text:"Nell lifts Encore. Encore allows it, with dignity. Under him, folded inside the green shawl: Celeste's script, warm and slightly furry."},{who:"NELL",text:"But *why*?"},{who:"STAGE",text:"Celeste points at the poster on the stage door. Felix crosses, and gently lifts the cream slip of paper. Underneath: NEVER."},{who:"FELIX",text:'*(reading)* "Twenty years on our stage, and she has never missed a show."'},{who:"CELESTE",text:'*(a whisper)* My voice went on Tuesday. *(she writes the rest)* "On Wednesday I could not even say thank you to Petra, so I wrote it. I hid my script. It was full of notes like *voice going, rest!* I gave Hugo the long speeches. If he was ready, nobody needed to know. —C."'},{who:"DEV",text:`It was on her card from the very first page. "I would shout it from the lamp room, if I could." She couldn't.`},{who:"HUGO",text:"Celeste. You could have just *told* me."},{who:"CELESTE",text:'*(writing)* "Yes, dear. That is the lesson. I am a slow learner. —C."'},{who:"TULLY",text:"*(arriving with more cocoa)* What did I miss?"},{who:"STAGE",text:"In the back row, Rosalind Ashe stands, and tears her notice in two."},{who:"ROSALIND ASHE",text:"A better second act than mine."}],v=[{who:"STAGE",beat:"setting",text:"Saturday, opening night. Every lantern in the Playhouse is lit."},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The kind ending",text:`Rosalind Ashe rewrites one scene overnight. The Keeper is now played by two people: the **Old Keeper** (Celeste), who climbs the ninety-nine steps and lights the lamp without a word, and the **Young Keeper** (Hugo), her memory of herself, who speaks the long speeches beside her. Rosalind's new line for the Old Keeper, written on a card she hands to Celeste: *"Some nights the lamp says it for me."* The audience stands at the end. Celeste has never missed a show. She just didn't speak in this one. Hugo bows exactly as she taught him.`},{who:"STAGE",beat:"Hugo's gran",text:"is in the front row after all. Matron has brought the whole of Harbour House in the minibus, and they clap loudest at the cat's part, which Rosalind has quietly written in. (Encore plays it asleep.)"},{who:"STAGE",beat:"Celeste's apology",text:'she writes cards to Hugo, to Petra and to the agency. Every one says "dear" and "simply" and ends "Your friend —C." The one to Petra says: "Thank you for keeping it. Simply the best friend a voice could have." The one to the agency comes with her green pen: "For the detective who read my handwriting better than I hid it."'},{who:"STAGE",beat:"Felix",text:`sits in the prompt corner with Petra all night, following the script with a finger, ready to whisper any forgotten line. Nobody forgets one. "It's perfect here," he whispers. "I can be in the show and nobody can see me." Quill makes a note. (Case 7 is coming.)`},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The arc beats",text:"**NEVER** goes into the Blot Ledger. It now reads **UNDER · THE · CLOCK · THAT · NEVER**."},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The arc beats",text:`**The postcard:** Asha puts Leela's list in order: 14 November, Fenwick bought; 2 February, Larkhill bought; 1 March, Fenwick closed; 9 June, Larkhill closed. "About four months from buying to closing," she says. "Both times." Dev spots the pattern in the signs: *The Larkhill Experience. The Fenwick Experience.* "What comes next on this list?" he reads. Nobody needs to say it. *The Inkwell Experience.* Asha pins the postcard to the Casebook Wall, next to the petition from Case 4.`},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The arc beats",text:`Dev, holding the Blot's card: "'A voice can be found on paper.' The Blot knew what this case was about before we did." Nell: "Hunch-o-meter: the Blot is on our side. Six." Quill: "Write it in pencil."`},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The running jokes",text:"Asha and Dev argue, in whispers, about whose turn it is to hold the torch in the wings. Petra shushes them. They keep arguing, more quietly."},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The running jokes",text:"**Biscuit** is found at the very top of the lighthouse set, sitting in the lamp room, wearing a sailor's cap from the props table. He gets a round of applause on his way down. Encore watches from the costume basket and does not clap."},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The office object",text:"Celeste's green pen goes on the shelf. Tap it to replay the case."},{who:"STAGE",beat:"The last chill",text:"As the audience files out, Encore stops washing his paw and stares at the very back row. One seat there is folded down, though nobody bought a ticket for it. Then, from somewhere above the empty seats, the same three notes on a violin, soft as a draught, and the prompt corner smells, just for a moment, of rosin. When Petra brings up the house lights, the seat has folded itself up again. Felix writes it down. Quill reads it twice."}],T={kind:"who-wrote",skill:"voice",title:"Who wrote this?",intro:"Three short notes appear with no names. The child drags each to Celeste, Hugo or Petra, then marks the word or habit that gave it away.",items:[{prompt:"Costumes, done. Lights, done. Cat: will not move.",answer:"Petra",options:["Celeste","Hugo","Petra"],tell:"a list."},{prompt:"sorry, sorry, i left my scarf in the wings. h",answer:"Hugo",options:["Celeste","Hugo","Petra"],tell:"lower case, sorry, small h."},{prompt:"Simply wonderful rehearsal, dear. Your friend —C.",answer:"Celeste",options:["Celeste","Hugo","Petra"],tell:"simply, dear, the sign-off."}],bonus:{prompt:"Bertie dear, simply the best soup! Your friend —",question:"Who wrote it, and what is missing?",answer:"Celeste",options:["Celeste","Hugo","Petra"],missing:"the C.",quill:"Everyone writes in their own voice. Listen with your eyes."}},S={backgrounds:["The open-air Playhouse: a curved bank of wooden seats under the sky, lanterns strung along the rows, the stage set as a tall striped lighthouse with a lamp room at the top, painted waves at its foot.","Backstage corridor: dressing-room doors (blank, with star shapes but no names), costume rails, ropes and sandbags, a big wicker costume basket.","Celeste's dressing room: a mirror ringed with bulbs, a cup of honey and lemon, a vase of sea lavender, an empty patch on the table where the script was.","The prompt corner: a small desk lit by a hooded lamp, the prompt book, cue sheets on a cork board, a headset.","The green room: comfortable, shabby, painted a warm orange (Felix's joke depends on it)."],props:["Celeste's script (with a green-ribboned cover)","Hugo's understudy script (page 12 open)","the cream note in green ink","Celeste's gull card","the poster with its removable cream slip (separate layer)","the calling card","the prompt book","Petra's clipboard and pencils","the green shawl","the costume basket","the honey-and-lemon cup","Leela's postcard (acacia trees and giraffes; sunbird stamp)","Biscuit's sailor's cap","Rosalind's face-down notice (blank side up)","Tully's bus ticket","the stage clock in the prompt corner"],portraits:["Hugo (six expressions)","Petra (six expressions)","Celeste (six expressions)","Encore (the cat's six: asleep, one-eye-open, offended, amused, smug, yawning)","Rosalind Ashe (small figure)","Sunny (small figure)"],documents:"the log on a clipboard; the note and the gull card in the same green handwriting font (big looping letters), so the match is visible as well as readable; Hugo's note in a quick lower-case font; the script page typed, with green underline strokes rendered by the app over live text.",fonts:{celeste:"green, looping, generous",hugo:"small, quick, lower case",petra:"small square capitals",leela:"slanting, travel-hurried, the same font as in Case 2"},notes:"Night, lamplit and cosy, never scary; a day variant of the Playhouse exterior for the map. Palette: the Playhouse world hue; deep teal night, golden lantern light, the warm red of the seats, and one accent of green (Celeste's ink and shawl) that the eye can follow from scene to scene. No lettering in any painting: poster, script, cards and dressing-room stars carry no painted words; all text is live. Diversity: the opening-night audience is mixed in age and colour, ordinary and various; keep the camera high so faces stay small. The violin beat is never painted as a figure: sound only (three soft notes), with the house lights coming up on empty seats; in the last chill one back-row seat is folded down, with nobody in it. The prompt corner must have a clear view of Celeste's dressing-room door (Petra can see it)."},x={script:"case-05.md",signedOffBy:"the owner (released at the owner's word, 8 Oct 2026)",signedOffOn:"2026-10-08"},C=[{id:"y1",tier:"easier",level:1,type:"punctuation",skill:"detail",strand:"sentence",objective:null,chapter:2,source:{doc:"5.S1.Q4",span:"hugo-note"},prompt:`Hugo wrote:
"i'll learn act two on the way home."
Which word must start with a capital letter?`,options:["learn","i'll","home"],answer:"i'll",explain:`"I" is always a capital letter, even inside "I'll". It also starts the sentence. Hugo writes in a hurry, with no capitals at all.`},{id:"y2",tier:"easier",level:1,type:"tense-sequence",skill:"sequence",strand:"reading",objective:null,chapter:1,source:{doc:"5.1",span:"log-honey"},prompt:"Look at Petra's log. Which of these happened first?",options:["Honey and lemon sent up","Celeste's script GONE!","Hugo in. Bus late."],answer:"Honey and lemon sent up",explain:"Petra writes a time at the start of each line. 5.45 comes before 7.00 and 7.15. So the honey and lemon went up first."},{id:"y3",tier:"easier",level:1,type:"vocab-in-context",skill:"voice",strand:"word",objective:"w10-clues",chapter:1,source:{doc:"5.1",span:"log-saving"},prompt:'Petra writes that Celeste "Whispers she is saving her voice". What does "saving" mean here?',options:["keeping it in a jar on her dressing table","using it very loudly","resting it so it lasts"],answer:"resting it so it lasts",explain:'"Saving" can mean keeping money. Here it means using something as little as you can, so it lasts. Celeste whispers to rest her voice.'},{id:"y4",tier:"easier",level:1,type:"pronoun",skill:"detail",strand:"sentence",objective:null,chapter:2,source:{doc:"5.S2.Q5",span:null},prompt:`Petra is asked where Encore is.
She says "He climbed in just before the light check."
Who is "he"?`,options:["Hugo, the understudy","Sunny","Encore"],answer:"Encore",explain:'Petra is answering a question about Encore. So "he" is Encore, the stage-door cat. A pronoun points back to someone already named.'},{id:"y5",tier:"easier",level:1,type:"fact-opinion",skill:"inference",strand:"reading",objective:null,chapter:1,source:{doc:"5.4",span:"card-simply"},prompt:"Which line from the card to Petra is an opinion?",options:["Simply splendid work on the storm scene!","The thunder made me jump.","The rain made me cry."],answer:"Simply splendid work on the storm scene!",explain:'"Splendid" is what the writer thinks of the work. That is an opinion. The other lines tell what happened.'},{id:"y6",tier:"at",level:2,type:"inference",skill:"inference",strand:"reading",objective:null,chapter:2,source:{doc:"5.S2.Q2",span:null},prompt:'Petra says "I use pencil. Pencil rubs out. Mistakes happen." Why does Petra choose pencil?',options:["because green ink is too dear to buy","so she can rub out mistakes","because she lost her pen"],answer:"so she can rub out mistakes",explain:"Petra gives her reasons one short sentence at a time. Pencil rubs out, and mistakes happen. So pencil lets her fix them. It also tells you she is careful."},{id:"y7",tier:"at",level:2,type:"vocab-in-context",skill:"voice",strand:"word",objective:"w10-meanings",chapter:1,source:{doc:"5.2",span:"note-simply"},prompt:`The note says:
"Learn the green lines tonight."
In a play, what are an actor's "lines"?`,options:["marks drawn with a ruler","people waiting in a queue","the words the actor says"],answer:"the words the actor says",explain:'"Lines" has more than one meaning. It can mean marks drawn with a pen, or a queue of people. In a play, your lines are the words you speak. The green lines are speeches marked in green.'},{id:"y8",tier:"at",level:2,type:"tense-sequence",skill:"sequence",strand:"reading",objective:null,chapter:1,source:{doc:"5.6",span:"pc-fenbuy"},prompt:"Leela's list is out of order. Which event on it happened first?",options:["14 November last year: Crane and Co buys Fenwick Library","2 February: Crane and Co buys Larkhill Library","1 March: Fenwick Library closes","9 June: Larkhill Library closes"],answer:"14 November last year: Crane and Co buys Fenwick Library",explain:'"Last year" is before every date this year. So the Fenwick buy comes first. Then Fenwick closes on 1 March. Larkhill follows the same pattern.'},{id:"y9",tier:"at",level:2,type:"punctuation",skill:"detail",strand:"sentence",objective:"s5-apostrophe",chapter:1,source:{doc:"5.1",span:"log-gone"},prompt:`Petra's log says "Celeste's script GONE!" What does the apostrophe in "Celeste's" show?`,options:["A letter has been left out.","The script belongs to Celeste.","There is more than one Celeste."],answer:"The script belongs to Celeste.",explain:`An apostrophe and "s" after a name shows that something belongs to that person. It is Celeste's script, so the script is hers.`},{id:"y10",tier:"at",level:2,type:"word-parts",skill:"detail",strand:"word",objective:"w6-build",chapter:2,source:{doc:"5.S2.Q2",span:null},prompt:`Petra says:
"Some actors say green is unlucky on stage."
What does the "un" in "unlucky" do?`,options:["It turns the word into its opposite.",'It makes the word mean "very", as in very lucky.','It makes the word mean "again".'],answer:"It turns the word into its opposite.",explain:'"Un" at the start of a word often means "not". Unlucky means not lucky. Think of unhappy, unkind and untidy.'},{id:"y11",tier:"harder",level:3,type:"figurative",skill:"inference",strand:"literature",objective:"li4-theme",chapter:1,source:{doc:"5.3",span:null},prompt:`In the play, the Keeper says:
"A ship we cannot see is still a ship."
What does the Keeper really mean?`,options:["Ships are very hard to see when a storm is coming.","The lamp at the top of the steps is broken.","Something can matter even when nobody sees it."],answer:"Something can matter even when nobody sees it.",explain:"The Keeper is not just talking about ships. The lamp helps sailors who will never say thank you. The play says good work matters even when no one notices it."},{id:"y12",tier:"harder",level:3,type:"sentence-combine",skill:"sequence",strand:"writing",objective:"s6-join",chapter:2,source:{doc:"5.S1.Q1",span:null},prompt:`Hugo says:
"The number four bus broke down by the bridge."
"I ran the rest of the way."
Which sentence joins them best?`,options:["The number four bus broke down by the bridge, although I ran the rest of the way.","The number four bus broke down by the bridge, so I ran the rest of the way.","Before the number four bus broke down by the bridge, I ran the rest of the way."],answer:"The number four bus broke down by the bridge, so I ran the rest of the way.",explain:'The bus breaking down is the reason Hugo gives for running. "So" joins a cause to what it made happen. "Although" and "before" change the meaning. (Whether the bus really broke down is another question.)'},{id:"y13",tier:"harder",level:3,type:"fact-opinion",skill:"inference",strand:"reading",objective:null,chapter:2,source:{doc:"5.S2.Q2",span:null},prompt:`Petra says:
"Some actors say green is unlucky on stage."
Which is the best way to describe this sentence?`,options:["It reports what some actors believe.","It proves that green ink brings bad luck to everybody on a stage.","It is Petra's own opinion about the colour green."],answer:"It reports what some actors believe.",explain:"It is true that some actors say this, and Petra is telling us so. But the idea that green brings bad luck is a belief, not a fact. Petra herself just uses pencil."},{id:"y14",tier:"harder",level:3,type:"voice",skill:"voice",strand:"writing",objective:null,chapter:5,source:{doc:"5.2",span:"note-dear"},prompt:'The green note starts "Hugo dear" and ends "Your friend —". Which other writer has the same way of writing?',options:["Hugo, in his note to Petra","Celeste, in her card to Petra","Petra, in her stage log for Friday"],answer:"Celeste, in her card to Petra",explain:`Writers leave fingerprints in their words. Celeste's card says "Petra dear", "Simply splendid" and "Your friend —C." The green note says "Hugo dear", "Simply all of them" and "Your friend —". Hugo writes with no capitals and says sorry twice.`},{id:"y15",tier:"harder",level:3,type:"voice",skill:"voice",strand:"writing",objective:"la6-register",chapter:5,source:{doc:"5.4",span:"card-simply"},prompt:"Which habits do the green note and Celeste's card share?",options:['"dear" after a name, "Simply", and "Your friend —"','no capital letters, and "sorry" said twice in a row',"a time written at the start of every single line"],answer:'"dear" after a name, "Simply", and "Your friend —"',explain:`Matching a writer's style is called matching their voice. Both pieces put "dear" after a name, both use "Simply", and both sign off "Your friend —". The other habits belong to Hugo's note and Petra's log.`},{id:"y16",tier:"harder",level:3,type:"inference",skill:"inference",strand:"reading",objective:null,chapter:5,source:{doc:"5.S4.Q2",span:"celeste-never"},prompt:`Celeste has whispered since Tuesday. She says:
"Twenty years, and I have not missed one show."
Why did she mark the long speeches for Hugo?`,options:["She wanted Hugo to forget his lines and fail on Saturday night.","She had forgotten every one of her lines.","Her voice is failing, and she is too proud to say so."],answer:"Her voice is failing, and she is too proud to say so.",explain:"She is proud of never missing a show. But she can only whisper, and long speeches need a strong voice. So she quietly gave them to Hugo, and kept it secret. It was kind, but a secret made everyone worried."}],E="The stage, ten to nine. The lighthouse lamp is dark. Petra brings up one soft light. Rosalind Ashe sits in the back row, her notice face down on her knee. Everyone waits.",A=[{where:"Chapter 1 — The scene (stage direction)",kind:"stage",text:"Friday, 8 pm, the night before opening. The Playhouse is open to the sky, and a sea wind keeps lifting the corners of the programmes on the empty seats. The lighthouse set stands on stage, its lamp dark. Backstage smells of paint, dust and honey-and-lemon. Somewhere above the stage a rope creaks against its pulley, slow as a clock."},{where:"End of chapter 1 (hook; the Blot is closer than you think)",kind:"hook",text:"The rosin on the calling card, and three notes on a violin from the empty seats. Played as the calling card's talk (doc 5.arc.card)."},{where:"Chapter 2 — Interviews (stage direction)",kind:"stage",text:"Interviews take place in the green room, which is not green. Felix points this out. Each answer arrives on the desk as a typed transcript. Outside the window, the painted lighthouse stands dark against a darker sky."},{where:"End of chapter 2 (hook; escalation: the deadline moves closer)",kind:"stage",who:"STAGE",text:"Rosalind Ashe comes down the aisle between the empty seats, a pencil in her hair and a sheet of paper in her hand. She pins the paper to the prompt-corner board, face down."},{where:"End of chapter 2 (hook; escalation: the deadline moves closer)",kind:"hook",who:"ROSALIND",text:"That's my notice for the stage door. It says *cancelled*. I'm not waiting for tomorrow. If I have no Keeper and no script at the nine o'clock run-through, I turn it over."},{where:"End of chapter 2 (hook; escalation: the deadline moves closer)",kind:"hook",who:"PETRA",direction:"looking at the stage clock",text:"Nine. That's fifty minutes."},{where:"End of chapter 2 (hook; escalation: the deadline moves closer)",kind:"stage",who:"STAGE",text:"In the costume basket, Encore begins, very loudly, to purr."},{where:"Chapter 3 — the impossible thing",kind:"impossible",text:'The script was on the table at six. Nobody went into the room. Petra searched it at seven, mirror to mat, and the script was not there. The only person who came out was Celeste, once, "with only her shawl over her arm". So how did a whole script leave a room that nobody entered? (The script went out inside the shawl. Answered in the reveal.)'},{where:"End of chapter 3 (hook; the false solution)",kind:"stage",who:"STAGE",text:"Constable Tully arrives, ten minutes behind, with the cocoa and a bus ticket."},{where:"End of chapter 3 (hook; the false solution)",kind:"hook",who:"TULLY",text:"Funny thing. Hugo says the number four broke down. I came here on the number four. It ran on time."},{where:"End of chapter 3 (hook; the false solution)",kind:"hook",who:"NELL",text:"He *lied*. So where was he between six and seven? In the wings, that's where, with nobody looking. He took the script, and Celeste's kind little note just made it easy for him. Hunch-o-meter: ten. Tully, the handcuffs."},{where:"End of chapter 3 (hook; the false solution)",kind:"hook",who:"TULLY",text:"I've only brought cocoa."},{where:"End of chapter 3 (hook; the false solution)",kind:"hook",who:"QUILL",text:"A lie about a bus is a lie about a bus. Ask him where he *was*."},{where:"End of chapter 3 (hook; the false solution)",kind:"stage",who:"STAGE",text:"In the wings, Hugo has gone the colour of the cream slip on the poster. Petra looks at the stage clock: half past eight."},{where:"Chapter 4 — The timeline (stage direction)",kind:"stage",text:"Before the first peg goes on, Hugo asks to speak. His sixth question unlocks (doc 5.S1.Q6), and it breaks the false solution."},{where:"End of chapter 4 (hook)",kind:"stage",who:"STAGE",text:"The last peg goes on. Petra looks up at the stage clock: ten to nine. Rosalind Ashe takes her seat in the back row with the notice face down on her knee. And on the dark stage, at the foot of the lighthouse, Celeste is already waiting, with her green pen and a stack of blank cards."},{where:"Chapter 5 — The accusation (stage direction)",kind:"stage",text:"The drawing-room reveal happens on the stage itself, under the dark lighthouse, the seats empty and lantern-lit. Hugo, Petra and Celeste stand in a row. Encore is carried on in the costume basket, because he will not be parted from it. Ten minutes to the run-through."},{where:"Mystery pass (6 Oct 2026)",kind:"note",text:`Stakes and clock: curtain up tomorrow at seven, moved by Rosalind to the nine o'clock run-through. Impossible thing: the script left a room nobody entered (inside the shawl). False solution: Hugo lied about the bus (ten), broken by Matron's sign-out. Clue in plain sight: "if I could" on Celeste's Wednesday card. Blot: rosin and three violin notes. Continuity: voice gone Tuesday, card written Wednesday; Hugo's note logged at 7.20.`}],W={format:1.1,id:e,number:5,title:t,label:o,level:2,world:n,setting:a,skills:s,vanishedWord:r,ledgerIndex:5,officeObject:i,arc:h,tutorial:l,card:d,cutscene:c,boardIntro:p,cast:u,docs:g,interviews:w,deductions:y,redHerrings:m,timeline:b,accusation:f,reveal:k,epilogue:v,drill:T,art:S,source:x,exercises:C,revealSetting:E,aside:A};export{f as accusation,h as arc,S as art,A as aside,p as boardIntro,d as card,u as cast,c as cutscene,y as deductions,W as default,g as docs,T as drill,v as epilogue,C as exercises,H as format,e as id,w as interviews,o as label,L as ledgerIndex,P as level,I as number,i as officeObject,m as redHerrings,k as reveal,E as revealSetting,a as setting,s as skills,x as source,b as timeline,t as title,l as tutorial,r as vanishedWord,n as world};
